WEBVTT

01:35.566 --> 01:37.319
It's over for you.

01:37.403 --> 01:39.198
Who the hell are these guys?

01:39.533 --> 01:42.246
I've never heard of Tenjiku.

01:42.329 --> 01:45.837
These guys
were never part of the past before.

01:55.480 --> 01:58.153
I bet you have no idea
what's going on.

01:59.155 --> 02:01.618
Let the Kanto Incident begin.

02:03.246 --> 02:06.335
Don't tell me he's...

02:06.962 --> 02:10.385
TOKYO REVENGERS

02:10.469 --> 02:13.809
TENJIKU
FIRST GENERATION, YOKOHAMA

02:13.893 --> 02:18.819
I used to be Captain of
Tokyo Manji Gang's Third Division,

02:18.903 --> 02:23.704
but now I'm General Staff Officer of
Yokohama's Tenjiku, Tetta Kisaki.

02:24.288 --> 02:26.960
General Staff Officer of Tenjiku?

02:28.171 --> 02:29.173
Why you...

02:29.758 --> 02:34.016
You mean you joined them
as soon as you got kicked out of Toman?

02:34.684 --> 02:39.235
Takemitchy, your mind
can't even begin to fathom me.

02:40.613 --> 02:43.702
I'm going to build my own Toman.

02:45.163 --> 02:46.542
Your own Toman?

02:47.794 --> 02:49.548
One day, Mikey

02:50.925 --> 02:53.263
will have no choice but to accept me.

02:53.346 --> 02:54.390
Ah...

02:54.473 --> 02:57.229
What's he talking about?
And what'd he mean

02:57.814 --> 02:59.108
by "hero"?

03:02.114 --> 03:03.116
Kisaki!

03:04.118 --> 03:05.955
Time to get going.

03:06.038 --> 03:07.291
It's Hanma!

03:10.255 --> 03:13.136
You're in a hell of a pinch, Takemitchy.

03:14.346 --> 03:16.518
But don't let it end here.

03:16.602 --> 03:18.271
Let's meet again.

03:23.574 --> 03:25.035
Kisaki...

03:27.957 --> 03:32.508
Hey, isn't Toman
made up of five divisions?

03:33.719 --> 03:35.096
Who's this guy?

03:35.723 --> 03:38.353
Do the other four suck this bad too?

03:42.069 --> 03:43.697
Toman ain't shit!

03:46.870 --> 03:48.164
Chifuyu!

03:48.749 --> 03:52.381
I got word we're brawling
with their Second Division in Shinjuku.

03:52.590 --> 03:54.385
I'm headed there.

03:54.803 --> 03:58.309
Make sure these guys
can never cause us trouble again.

03:58.393 --> 04:01.315
I should have stayed home.

04:01.399 --> 04:02.484
Listen up!

04:03.027 --> 04:06.409
Crush Toman before
that bastard Kakucho shows up.

04:06.952 --> 04:09.373
We, Team Mochizuki,
will get all the glory.

04:10.166 --> 04:12.588
I'll leave these punks in your hands.

04:12.672 --> 04:13.841
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

04:17.640 --> 04:21.105
This isn't a fight. It's a lynching!

04:22.190 --> 04:24.445
Tenjiku's going to sic
all these guys on us

04:24.529 --> 04:26.240
when we're already beaten to a pulp?

04:27.033 --> 04:28.453
Akkun.

04:28.537 --> 04:30.875
Takemichi, escape when you get the chance.

04:32.169 --> 04:35.885
I won't stand for these jerks
to defeat everyone in the First Division.

04:36.177 --> 04:38.473
Holy shit! I want to run.

04:38.557 --> 04:41.605
I was so looking forward
to reading next week's comics.

04:41.688 --> 04:42.982
We've got to protect Takemichi!

04:43.065 --> 04:45.320
Got that, Makoto and Yamagishi?

04:48.660 --> 04:51.081
- Huh?
- What's wrong?

04:51.625 --> 04:53.127
Bikes are ramming into us!

04:57.052 --> 04:59.056
It's the Meguro's Twin Devils!

04:59.641 --> 05:01.227
What the hell?

05:01.310 --> 05:02.939
Run!

05:03.022 --> 05:04.358
They're going to run us down!

05:06.153 --> 05:07.197
Help!

05:07.447 --> 05:08.575
We're going to die!

05:14.838 --> 05:16.675
What's up, First Division?

05:18.344 --> 05:21.225
These... These guys are insane.

05:21.893 --> 05:24.022
You goddamn bastard!

05:30.786 --> 05:32.080
Holy...

05:33.165 --> 05:37.465
Is this guy
Fourth Division Captain Nahoya Kawata?

05:37.550 --> 05:42.935
Wait. I thought Nahoya was always smiling.

05:43.562 --> 05:45.231
Look at that.

05:46.651 --> 05:47.778
Takuya?

05:49.239 --> 05:51.995
I found him lying in the street,
so I picked him up.

05:52.078 --> 05:55.586
He's injured,
so make sure you get him to a hospital.

05:55.669 --> 05:57.590
Uh, sure.

05:57.673 --> 05:58.884
I'm worried about him.

05:59.468 --> 06:02.725
He's angry,
but he sure is kind.

06:02.808 --> 06:05.104
Hey, hey, Takemitchy.

06:06.775 --> 06:08.402
That guy ain't me.

06:08.486 --> 06:09.572
What?

06:09.656 --> 06:11.367
There's two Nahoyas?

06:13.412 --> 06:15.918
- Didn't you know that?
- Huh?

06:16.001 --> 06:18.172
Even their hair colors are different.

06:18.256 --> 06:20.260
- Huh?
- We're saved!

06:20.343 --> 06:23.600
Huh? I think there's someone
caught on my wheel.

06:24.727 --> 06:26.982
The smiling one
with the heart of a demon is

06:27.566 --> 06:29.862
the older brother, aka Smiley.

06:30.614 --> 06:33.411
All you guys,
get checked out at a hospital.

06:33.494 --> 06:35.582
The angry-looking one
with a heart of gold is...

06:36.166 --> 06:39.924
- You guys, too.
- ...the younger brother, aka Angry.

06:40.216 --> 06:41.385
There.

06:41.803 --> 06:45.644
They're the Captain
and Vice-Captain of the Fourth Division.

06:46.186 --> 06:47.355
What?

06:47.439 --> 06:49.902
The captains of
the Fourth Division are twins?

06:49.986 --> 06:53.284
What's your deal?
You've been in Toman longer than us.

06:53.367 --> 06:56.624
Mocchi's going to Shinjuku, huh?
We're going too, right?

06:56.708 --> 07:00.591
Yeah,
but I'd like to outfox them.

07:01.300 --> 07:03.012
Chifuyu, can you stand?

07:03.555 --> 07:04.640
Sure can.

07:04.724 --> 07:06.060
Chifuyu!

07:06.644 --> 07:09.441
Takemitchy and Chifuyu, ride on back.

07:09.525 --> 07:11.361
Oh, uh, sure.

07:13.157 --> 07:14.535
Hold on tight.

07:14.952 --> 07:17.750
Let's go raid Yokohama.

07:18.334 --> 07:20.213
Time for a counterattack, huh?

07:20.296 --> 07:22.050
Huh? A raid?

07:27.352 --> 07:29.189
Take care of Takuya!

07:34.742 --> 07:36.579
- Hey!
- Yeah?

07:36.663 --> 07:39.585
Are we really going to
raid Yokohama right now?

07:39.669 --> 07:43.552
You'd better believe it.
We'll be like bam ka-pow to Tenjiku.

07:44.177 --> 07:45.681
"Bam ka-pow"?

07:45.764 --> 07:47.392
What's he talking about?

07:47.475 --> 07:48.477
HOMAGE TO AMIDA BUDDHA

07:48.562 --> 07:49.856
Anyway, Chifuyu.

07:49.981 --> 07:52.235
Mocchi beat your ass, right?

07:52.695 --> 07:55.283
What? He didn't beat me.

07:55.408 --> 07:58.414
He just sucker-punched me. That's all.

07:58.497 --> 08:00.376
He definitely didn't beat me.

08:00.459 --> 08:02.590
I'm ready for a revenge match right now.

08:02.673 --> 08:06.263
You were out cold until just now.
Don't push yourself.

08:06.346 --> 08:08.727
Don't act tough, Chifuyu.

08:08.810 --> 08:12.860
Mocchi's a freaking beast, man.
Even we lost to him.

08:12.943 --> 08:13.987
What?

08:14.070 --> 08:18.580
You both lost to him?
Is that Mocchi guy that tough?

08:18.663 --> 08:22.880
Yeah. He's been our perpetual enemy
even before we joined Toman.

08:23.548 --> 08:26.261
Back when we formed the Twin Devils gang,

08:26.345 --> 08:30.979
we got in tons of brawls with
the Jugem gang from Kawasaki.

08:32.524 --> 08:35.656
Neither of our gangs
could defeat the other.

08:36.532 --> 08:40.540
Let's settle this with
a one-on-one between us captains.

08:41.709 --> 08:43.170
Bring it on.

08:44.130 --> 08:45.884
KANJI MOCHIZUKI
KAWASAKI JUGEM LEADER

08:49.224 --> 08:51.061
He kicked my ass.

08:52.230 --> 08:55.278
Then I challenged him, but got beaten too.

08:55.361 --> 08:57.866
You got knocked out cold, Angry.

08:58.075 --> 09:00.246
And you were frothing
at the mouth.

09:00.371 --> 09:04.170
How can you enjoy
talking about a defeat so much?

09:04.547 --> 09:06.008
Doesn't it piss you off?

09:06.383 --> 09:09.180
We don't pick fights we can win.

09:09.306 --> 09:12.228
Just like you, Takemitchy.

09:13.606 --> 09:17.656
Anyway, since Tenjiku's sent out
their main powerhouse Mocchi,

09:17.740 --> 09:20.746
Toman's got to raid them now.

09:20.871 --> 09:23.334
- Look, Smiley.
- Huh?

09:24.545 --> 09:25.672
Tenjiku guys.

09:25.756 --> 09:29.137
Hey, hey. Speak of the devil,
or something like that.

09:32.686 --> 09:34.523
Get off, Takemitchy.

09:34.607 --> 09:35.859
Huh?

09:35.942 --> 09:37.070
Oh, right.

09:40.076 --> 09:43.499
We're going to question these guys
about Tenjiku's hideout.

09:43.583 --> 09:46.798
You guys wait here for us. Sorry.

09:50.597 --> 09:52.100
We got a question for you!

09:52.183 --> 09:55.064
That's more like torture than questioning.

09:55.147 --> 09:56.859
Hold up, assholes!

09:56.943 --> 09:58.362
We just want to talk!

09:59.865 --> 10:01.619
- Chifuyu.
- Huh?

10:03.122 --> 10:04.750
I saw Kisaki.

10:04.834 --> 10:05.961
What?

10:06.044 --> 10:10.469
I bet it was him
who planned Tenjiku's attack.

10:10.554 --> 10:12.265
What?! Really?

10:12.348 --> 10:13.977
Why him?

10:14.060 --> 10:16.566
I don't know. But...

10:17.818 --> 10:23.454
I think I've figured out something
that's been bugging me for a long time.

10:23.538 --> 10:25.040
You figured out something?

10:25.709 --> 10:27.420
It's always seemed so weird.

10:28.422 --> 10:30.927
No matter how many times I try, I fail.

10:32.639 --> 10:35.604
Draken was saved, but I failed.

10:36.981 --> 10:41.072
Kisaki and BLACK DRAGON were
driven out of Toman, but I failed.

10:41.657 --> 10:45.247
No matter what I did,
the future never got better.

10:45.790 --> 10:47.001
Why?

10:47.920 --> 10:49.005
Chifuyu...

10:50.675 --> 10:52.053
What if...

10:52.638 --> 10:56.019
After I change the future,

10:56.102 --> 10:59.652
what if there's someone else
who changes it even more?

10:59.735 --> 11:00.779
Huh?

11:00.862 --> 11:05.622
What if Kisaki
can also travel through time?

11:05.705 --> 11:06.874
Huh.

11:07.793 --> 11:10.882
That's totally ridiculous! There's no way!

11:10.966 --> 11:13.011
But the truth is, I travel through time.

11:13.721 --> 11:16.309
So it wouldn't be crazy
if someone else could too.

11:16.936 --> 11:19.567
Well, yeah. Maybe so...

11:20.317 --> 11:22.990
Remember what you told me
at the bathhouse?

11:23.490 --> 11:24.535
Oh...

11:24.618 --> 11:28.877
You mean about how Mikey needed Kisaki?

11:28.960 --> 11:30.045
Mm.

11:30.964 --> 11:35.431
With Kisaki out of Toman,
Mikey took on all of Toman's darkness.

11:35.932 --> 11:38.145
So he turned out like that 12 years later.

11:39.815 --> 11:41.109
That's what I believed.

11:42.779 --> 11:46.913
I believed that was
why I couldn't change the future.

11:47.496 --> 11:50.336
Hey there, hero.

11:51.296 --> 11:52.925
But I was wrong.

11:54.260 --> 11:56.974
There's no way Mikey would need Kisaki.

11:57.726 --> 12:00.732
What's more, Kisaki's remained consistent.

12:01.399 --> 12:02.569
I'm going to...

12:02.653 --> 12:04.405
Kisaki has always...

12:05.533 --> 12:07.453
...build my own Toman.

12:07.954 --> 12:12.338
...tried to build a Toman
that does what he wants.

12:14.050 --> 12:16.054
What Tenjiku's doing now is also...

12:16.137 --> 12:22.108
You mean Kisaki's come from
the future over and over again like you

12:22.191 --> 12:25.406
and is remaking Toman to suit him?

12:27.201 --> 12:28.453
I'll admit,

12:29.038 --> 12:34.508
that would explain why you keep failing
no matter how many times you try.

12:35.802 --> 12:40.352
If all of it was
just as Kisaki planned it...

12:54.798 --> 12:57.721
My hero.

12:59.432 --> 13:02.271
I'll make him pay.

13:10.120 --> 13:11.749
Hey, Takemitchy.

13:13.503 --> 13:15.673
I get why you're so upset.

13:16.509 --> 13:19.515
If everything I'd worked my ass off to fix

13:19.598 --> 13:23.898
got screwed up every time by Kisaki,
I'd be pissed too.

13:25.400 --> 13:26.904
But you know, Takemitchy.

13:30.410 --> 13:32.456
Quit making that face.

13:34.210 --> 13:35.379
Chifuyu?

13:35.462 --> 13:38.553
Man, you look like this.

13:39.972 --> 13:44.146
If I were in your shoes,
I'd probably be like that too.

13:45.399 --> 13:47.612
But is Kisaki right here now?

13:47.696 --> 13:49.783
Can you see him right now?

13:50.660 --> 13:54.626
What's important now is figuring out
what the deal with Tenjiku is.

13:55.168 --> 13:57.924
Even more so
if Kisaki's pulling the strings.

13:59.051 --> 14:03.686
If Kisaki can also travel time,
then he's getting desperate now.

14:03.769 --> 14:06.817
What? He's getting desperate too?

14:06.901 --> 14:10.157
I mean, he died in the future, right?

14:11.451 --> 14:12.704
That's right!

14:13.204 --> 14:16.670
So that means
he can't go back to the future.

14:20.427 --> 14:22.891
This time, he's failed too.

14:23.768 --> 14:27.316
Unless we first find out
if Kisaki can travel through time,

14:27.399 --> 14:29.195
we won't get anywhere.

14:30.322 --> 14:32.409
Kisaki's in Tenjiku.

14:32.994 --> 14:35.040
He might be at their hideout.

14:35.123 --> 14:36.627
Hey!

14:37.169 --> 14:39.925
We found out where Tenjiku's hideout is.

14:40.008 --> 14:41.260
We're going in!

14:59.255 --> 15:01.050
It's a big world out there.

15:02.302 --> 15:05.058
Never thought there was
a monster like you in it.

15:05.643 --> 15:08.899
Guess even Toman's got someone with balls.

15:10.570 --> 15:12.824
Now things are getting fun.

15:13.743 --> 15:17.249
This guy's Mochizuki,
who used to be in Jugem.

15:17.751 --> 15:18.961
Hey, Mocchi.

15:22.051 --> 15:24.472
Don't keep all the fun for yourself.

15:24.556 --> 15:26.017
The Haitani Brothers?

15:35.368 --> 15:37.582
Gotcha, Mitsuya.

15:38.751 --> 15:40.797
Sorry about the cheap shot.

15:40.963 --> 15:45.263
Who the hell said you could
steal my kill, you sons of bitches!

15:45.848 --> 15:48.228
You always hog the spotlight.

15:48.813 --> 15:50.440
And strike a dumb pose.

15:50.900 --> 15:53.321
Who the hell cares who took him out?

15:54.658 --> 15:58.666
Toman's not a gang that can be crushed
if we stick to your kind of thinking.

15:59.250 --> 16:02.214
We've got to attack now
while their guard's down.

16:02.674 --> 16:04.678
Let's finish this today.

16:08.351 --> 16:11.149
It's not just the ex-leader of Jugem,

16:11.608 --> 16:14.614
but they've even got
the goddamn Haitani Brothers with them.

16:15.198 --> 16:17.411
Tenjiku is serious shit.

16:18.664 --> 16:20.417
SHIBUYA CENTER STREET

16:21.002 --> 16:23.423
Hey, shouldn't somebody stop them?

16:23.507 --> 16:24.676
Then you go do it.

16:24.759 --> 16:28.099
- Where are the cops?
- They'll kill them.

16:40.165 --> 16:41.585
Next.

16:41.668 --> 16:43.797
SHION MADARAME, TENJIKU'S BIG FOUR
THE NINTH GENERATION BLACK DRAGON LEADER

16:49.308 --> 16:51.479
Who the hell are you people?

16:51.563 --> 16:53.525
Huh?

17:11.185 --> 17:15.695
A lot more guys here than I expected.
Not really a hideout. More like...

17:15.778 --> 17:17.322
A clubhouse.

17:17.406 --> 17:20.579
Holy shit! There are at least 100 of them!

17:20.663 --> 17:21.707
Huh?

17:22.291 --> 17:24.504
You finally showed up, Toman.

17:24.587 --> 17:26.883
"BRAWLER" KAKUCHO
TENJIKU'S BIG FOUR

17:26.967 --> 17:29.639
Huh? We "finally showed up"?

17:29.723 --> 17:31.434
They've been waiting for us.

17:31.518 --> 17:33.062
Ooh.

17:33.146 --> 17:35.025
Let's see who gets the most kills.

17:36.027 --> 17:38.323
You've got to be kidding.
Just four dudes?

17:38.406 --> 17:39.659
Huh?

17:43.834 --> 17:46.088
Hey, you guys get out of here.

17:49.345 --> 17:52.100
I told you to get out.

17:52.184 --> 17:53.227
Are you deaf?

17:54.146 --> 17:55.566
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

18:04.542 --> 18:06.087
What's going on here?

18:14.061 --> 18:17.985
Originally, I wasn't going to fight fair.

18:18.069 --> 18:19.446
But I changed my mind.

18:20.407 --> 18:22.202
I'll fight all of you alone.

18:24.081 --> 18:27.295
Oh, really?
Think you're cool, don't you, asshole?

18:28.715 --> 18:33.349
I'm Tokyo Manji Gang
Fourth Division's Captain, Nahoya Kawata.

18:33.433 --> 18:35.938
If you're fighting solo, then so am I.

18:36.021 --> 18:38.192
- Nahoya!
- Hey, that's not fair!

18:38.276 --> 18:39.612
Go for it, Smiley!

18:40.196 --> 18:42.869
I'm Kakucho, one of Tenjiku's Big Four.

18:42.952 --> 18:46.793
Sorry, but the first guy
I want to beat the shit out of is

18:46.877 --> 18:50.551
Tokyo Manji Gang's First Division Captain,

18:50.634 --> 18:52.262
Takemichi Hanagaki!

18:52.763 --> 18:54.308
- What?
- Oh.

18:55.477 --> 18:57.022
I've heard the rumors.

18:57.105 --> 19:01.990
First Division's Captain means
you're the toughest of all of you, right?

19:03.242 --> 19:04.621
Uh, actually,

19:04.704 --> 19:06.165
that's not really true.

19:06.373 --> 19:09.296
He fights with his kindness,
not his fists.

19:09.379 --> 19:10.633
Takemitchy!

19:11.300 --> 19:14.348
I can't let things end here.

19:14.431 --> 19:18.147
I don't care if he's one of
Tenjiku's Big Four, I'm not going to lose.

19:26.915 --> 19:29.169
You want to escape
into the sea too?

19:29.253 --> 19:30.421
Yeah.

19:31.131 --> 19:34.263
Swim, swim, swim.

19:34.346 --> 19:36.141
In the Taiyaki-kun song,

19:37.102 --> 19:38.855
how do things end for it?

19:40.316 --> 19:42.530
I don't know. I forgot.

19:52.299 --> 19:53.844
Nice bike

19:54.344 --> 19:55.388
you got there.

19:58.477 --> 19:59.479
Thanks.

20:03.112 --> 20:04.991
I'm Izana Kurokawa.

20:08.874 --> 20:09.959
See you around.

20:11.713 --> 20:12.840
Hm.

20:13.926 --> 20:15.763
You can do it, Takemitchy!

20:17.892 --> 20:18.977
Wait!

20:19.646 --> 20:22.943
I get the feeling
I've seen this guy before.

20:28.037 --> 20:31.628
- Oh shit. This guy's tough.
- Yeah.

20:31.711 --> 20:33.924
Be careful, Takemitchy!

20:34.007 --> 20:35.719
Focus, Takemitchy!

20:37.765 --> 20:38.975
Bring it on.

20:53.922 --> 20:55.341
- Yes!
- He did it! Awesome!

20:55.425 --> 20:58.222
A lucky head-on punch!

20:58.598 --> 20:59.684
What?

21:01.980 --> 21:05.904
Th... That's the first time
I knocked down a hoodlum with one punch!

21:05.988 --> 21:09.161
You really stole the show
with that one, Takemitchy!

21:09.244 --> 21:10.539
- When did I...
- You did it!

21:11.457 --> 21:13.210
...get so good?

21:19.139 --> 21:20.266
Huh?

21:20.934 --> 21:24.984
Damn it! That pisses me off, Takemichi!

21:25.569 --> 21:27.948
Then I'll avenge you.

21:28.658 --> 21:29.869
Kaku-chan!

21:32.499 --> 21:33.835
Kaku-chan?

21:33.919 --> 21:35.254
- Huh?
- Huh?

21:35.338 --> 21:38.427
About time you realized, Dummy-michi.

21:39.095 --> 21:40.724
Haven't seen you since second grade.

21:40.808 --> 21:43.688
Oh yeah! You moved away.

21:43.772 --> 21:46.736
How you been? Kind of weird to ask though.

21:47.320 --> 21:49.199
You haven't changed, Kaku-chan.

21:49.575 --> 21:51.663
You've always gotten into fights.

21:52.122 --> 21:55.127
Same goes for you. You're as weak as ever.

21:56.463 --> 21:57.925
You aren't much better.

21:58.718 --> 22:00.514
Where'd you get that scar?

22:00.597 --> 22:01.766
Screw you!

22:02.560 --> 22:04.522
I'm actually damn tough.

22:04.605 --> 22:06.985
I lost on purpose just now.

22:07.611 --> 22:10.241
You haven't changed since then either.

22:11.953 --> 22:13.915
You were my hero.

22:15.878 --> 22:18.675
Takemichi, there's something
I want to ask you.

22:18.758 --> 22:20.011
Huh?

22:20.721 --> 22:23.643
What kind of guy is that Tetta Kisaki?

22:25.438 --> 22:27.483
Why did he get kicked out of Toman?

22:29.780 --> 22:32.870
He tried to take over Toman, but failed.

22:34.039 --> 22:35.207
I see.

22:36.376 --> 22:38.715
Kaku-chan,
I've got a favor to ask you too.

22:38.798 --> 22:39.800
Hm?

22:40.384 --> 22:42.263
Help me see Kisaki.

22:43.474 --> 22:47.357
There's something
that I've just got to find out from him.

22:48.317 --> 22:50.822
Sorry, but I'm not obliged to help you.

22:52.283 --> 22:57.210
My hero now is the leader of Tenjiku,
Izana Kurokawa.

22:57.293 --> 22:58.505
Huh?

22:58.588 --> 23:01.636
I've devoted my life to him.

23:04.600 --> 23:06.980
In other words, you and I

23:07.982 --> 23:09.484
are enemies.

23:10.612 --> 23:11.739
Kaku-chan...

23:12.240 --> 23:17.166
Kisaki is Tenjiku's General Staff Officer,
so he's close to Izana.

23:18.252 --> 23:20.632
You'll have to attack
if you want to see him.

23:23.847 --> 23:24.932
Takemichi.

23:26.853 --> 23:29.482
Beware of a traitor.

23:29.567 --> 23:30.610
Huh?

23:40.046 --> 23:41.966
A traitor?

23:42.885 --> 23:44.889
Translated by Brian Athey
